<!-- Jonathan confirmed attributes are OK to be used as UM can still manipulate them if needed. -->

<!--

Requirements:
- Configurable system fields for components and pages
  - Force the installation/site to have more/less mandatory fields
- Mandatory basic properties per control
- New types of objects

-->

<!--

Recommendation:
	- "Crawl":
		- Implement only control/data-source listing via proposal A (i.e. existing functionality).
	- "Walk":
		- Implement overrides.
	- "Run":
		- 🚀 Sky is not the limit.
	- Consider allowing only extending the descriptors and not overriding them to protect ourselves. Or pick what's overridable.
		- Overriding certain properties like display-template, no-template-required, merge-strategy can be break things, there's associated code.
		- Extending or overriding control properties is not currently supported via configuration; we have freedom to choose.
	- Two main aspects: Listing, and Properties
		- Control/DS Listing: Proposal "A" allows for the cleanest configuration (less verbose) while maintaining current site-config-tools.xml functionality.
		- Control/DS Properties/Form: Proposal "A" allows for the cleanest configuration (less verbose) while allowing to override control descriptor stuff.

Control Listing:

	Proposal A:
	- The TypeBuilder app has its defaults in the code. No configuration is needed.
	- To exclude a control, <controlExclusions>aws-file-upload</controlExclusions> or <controls id="aws-file-upload" exclude="true" />

	Proposal B:
	- The TypeBuilder app will render only the controls listed in the configuration.

Control Properties/Form:

	- Code defaults.

	Proposal A:
	- If a <descriptor/> tag is present, the descriptor is deep merged/mixed with the code file descriptor.
		- This would allow overriding ANYTHING and EVERYTHING
		- To remove a property, set it to "null".

	Proposal B:
	- If a <descriptor/> tag is present, the descriptor overrides with the code file descriptor.
		- This would allow overriding ANYTHING and EVERYTHING
		- To remove a property, simply omit.
		- Very verbose as it requires defining the complete descriptor. Easy to miss/mess something.

-->

<!--
=========================================================
(Default Config) or (Upgraded site without plugins):
=========================================================
